{"skill":{"slug":"ai-ppt-generator","displayName":"Baidu Wenku AIPPT"},"version":{"version":"1.1.5","createdAt":1775033369430,"changelog":"- Skill name updated from \"ai-ppt-generator\" to \"Baidu Wenku AIPPT\"\n- Description clarified to reference \"Baidu Wenku AI\" instead of just \"Baidu AI\"\n- No changes to scripts, features, or core functionality\n- No file changes detected in this version","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"_meta.json","size":135,"sha256":"b0d4b72504836745508fe4fdd476c38a4b59ef230c39df4a2bfdb7aed1e35e1a","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3311,"sha256":"4e8a2cf7f73248d5a7053f24d300a91e37495e96ea1a3bcec362492e812b2920","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/generate_ppt.py","size":5171,"sha256":"bb587899e8ddedf0ff09d2a4ebeb484135c53aac6ddeeaaa9cd7d3745c847776","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/random_ppt_theme.py","size":12328,"sha256":"badb623bf3035196edad3a332bf428bbc0d16fd04a14a32a2c0f22ffaa0fcedf","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/ppt_theme_list.py","size":1260,"sha256":"b3a614ebd5855a56f4f4126b74a271f95342bf8a1b825c6727c42cca6b5745be","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2019,"sha256":"18bc2787b5a590ab02fb6ee22dc4b0b0b5df7d5a979dd1339079b6ba232a8ee0","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789038530543,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"cf496a0f95e07c6686091dfc91078629cebc19d918e43e6bf56b1399175c12fd","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/cf496a0f95e07c6686091dfc91078629cebc19d918e43e6bf56b1399175c12fd","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ai-ppt-generator\nVersion: 1.1.5\n\nThe skill bundle is a legitimate integration with the Baidu Wenku AI PPT generation service. The scripts (generate_ppt.py, ppt_theme_list.py, and random_ppt_theme.py) correctly use the BAIDU_API_KEY to interact with official Baidu Qianfan endpoints (qianfan.baidubce.com). The workflow is transparent, and the use of subprocess.Popen in random_ppt_theme.py is implemented safely using argument lists, preventing shell injection.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162081884},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":13,"checkedAt":1789038530543},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill does what it claims: it uses Baidu's PPT API to generate presentations from user-provided topics, with no hidden persistence or unrelated local data access found.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access and BAIDU_API_KEY use are proportionate to Baidu API integration, and the scripts do not scan broad local files or collect unrelated environment data.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill metadata declares python3 and BAIDU_API_KEY requirements; no installer, dependency download, or post-install execution behavior was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The agent workflow asks for a topic and template preference before running scripts; content is sent to Baidu as part of the core function, but the privacy disclosure could be more explicit.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanisms, scheduled tasks, memory writes, tool replacement, privilege escalation, destructive actions, or background workers were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Baidu AI PPT generation, and the code calls Baidu Qianfan AI PPT endpoints to list themes, generate an outline, and generate the final PPT.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending your PPT topic and any optional web content to Baidu's API using your BAIDU_API_KEY. Avoid submitting secrets, private business plans, regulated data, or other sensitive content unless your Baidu account and policies allow that use.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The scanner concern about smart versus random template selection is downgraded because the skill explicitly documents random fallback and uses random selection only for choosing a template style, not for hidden behavior.\n[LP3] expected: Python execution, network calls, and BAIDU_API_KEY access are expected for this API-backed generator; no broader permission use was found in the artifacts.\n[SQP-2] expected: The user's topic, generated outline, title, and optional web_content are sent to Baidu; this is central to the advertised Baidu AI generation workflow, though users should be warned not to submit sensitive material.\n[E1] expected: The external POST requests target the documented Baidu AI PPT workflow and are not accompanied by evidence of unrelated exfiltration.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess call invokes the bundled generate_ppt.py with an explicit argument list and shell is not enabled, so the flagged command-injection concern is not supported by the inspected code.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese template categories and messages fit the Baidu Wenku-oriented workflow and are a usability/localization limitation rather than a security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789038530543}}}}}